  },
  "description": "DAPCII crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C112 H220 Co8 N4 O72 P8 Tb8,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 8 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 9 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 8 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 9 O neighbors; Co4A (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Tb5? (Tb) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 23 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.486-4.312 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.58-150.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoII8TbIII8(μ3-OH)4(NO3)4(O3P tBu)8(O2C tBu)16]·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
